diff --git a/tests/nv2a_bindings/README.md b/tests/nv2a_bindings/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6c5a07f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/nv2a_bindings/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+# Renderer binding regression
+
+This fixture includes the production D3D11 renderer and checks real driver
+bindings and GPU pixels. Run it from the repository's activated tool environment:
+
+```powershell
+cmake -S tools/xboxrecomp/tests/nv2a_bindings -B conformance_tmp/stutter-bindings-test -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
+cmake --build conformance_tmp/stutter-bindings-test
+ctest --test-dir conformance_tmp/stutter-bindings-test --output-on-failure
+```
+
+The nineteen cases cover fixed vertex resources, changing shader constants, raw and
+index ring wraps, failed uploads, resize/reset, pixel shader/sampler bindings,
+and cached topology/rasterizer/scissor/blend/depth-stencil states. Independent
+unconditional setter sequences provide reference images across ordinary draws,
+shader clears, color/depth Y16 conversion, blits and composition.
+
+Pipeline cases inspect the actual IA/RS/OM getters, check zero setter calls for
+unchanged draws, and exercise state-table eviction while objects remain bound,
+`ClearState` invalidation, NULL states, NULL versus four-one blend factors,
+changed blend factors/sample masks/stencil references, and zero/multiple scissor
+rectangles. Full stencil arguments are checked before driver conversion. They
+also verify that pipeline setter counters advance only with profiling enabled.
+
+Color-write cases exercise real 1x/4x MSAA resolves, Y16 views, generated mipmaps
+and swizzled rendered mip chains. Submitted depth/stencil draws and clears with
+no color channels enabled preserve exact color pixels and reuse those views;
+real color writes refresh the affected resources. Injected PS/raw/index/vertex
+constant and clear-constant Map failures submit no stale draw, preserve color
+generations and pixels, and remain retryable with the same state.
+
+Sequential-index cases compare the production non-indexed `Draw` with actual
+`DrawIndexed` using an independent immutable identity index buffer and the same
+pipeline and raw vertices. They exercise vertex programs and pretransformed
+positions, nonzero guest index offsets, points/lines/triangles, six auxiliary
+paths, raw/index ring wraps, reset and 1x/4x MSAA. Flat-shaded, permuted and
+duplicate-index lists retain the indexed path; varying vertex colors verify
+the guest's last-vertex provoking rule. Genuine index-Map failures use a
+nonidentity list, while direct draws leave the index ring and its pending
+failure injection untouched. Profile counters count index-Map attempts and
+omissions only with profiling enabled.
