diff --git a/tests/nv2a_slow_frame/README.md b/tests/nv2a_slow_frame/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..51224a6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/nv2a_slow_frame/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Bounded slow-frame attribution
+
+`RECOMP_SLOW_FRAME_TRACE=1` enables a renderer-thread accumulator. It emits
+`[HITCH] phase=slow_frame` only for flip intervals strictly over 30 ms, at
+most once every 500 ms and at most 64 times per process. It adds no host
+clock reads when disabled and stops timing when the record budget is spent.
+Enable it only for a diagnostic pass; timing every Map/Unmap adds overhead.
+
+Trace boundaries use the exact QPC read used for the corresponding frame CSV
+row. Raw start/end ticks and frequency avoid decimal rounding ambiguity;
+`csv_line=0` means no CSV was enabled. The intervals describe guest flip
+completion, not display scanout. Loading, menus and paused time are included.
+
+Raw vertex, index and constant-buffer Map/Unmap totals include counts, byte
+requests, upload modes, failures, maxima and HRESULTs. Draw and readback scope
+totals **include** their nested API work. Present API, pacing wait, capture
+probe and capture I/O are separately named. Observed readback-pending wall
+time overlaps CPU work and is clipped to each interval; it is not GPU time.
+Do not add nested/overlapping totals or infer causality from overlap alone.
+Formatting and log I/O belong to the following interval and are accumulated
+there as `diagnostic_output`. Failed clocks retain API counters and increment
+`timing_invalid`, without changing API execution or guest RAM ordering.
+
+This deterministic fixture checks disabled clocks, exact boundaries,
+Map/Unmap metadata, pending overlap, rate/budget limits and failed clocks.
+The `nv2a_shader_lookup` fixture additionally checks actual D3D11 upload
+failure/retry and copied bytes, plus CSV/trace boundary integration.
