diff --git a/tests/nv2a_world_lighting/README.md b/tests/nv2a_world_lighting/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5e4aec6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/nv2a_world_lighting/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,126 @@
+# Native local lighting GPU regressions
+
+The executables include the production D3D11 renderer, create a real GPU device,
+draw through its public clear/draw paths, and read back rendered pixels. CTest
+runs each at 1x/4x MSAA and render scale 1/3, using both generic and specialized
+pixel shaders; no game assets are required. Specialized runs wait for the exact
+draw's shader to compile before submitting it, so asynchronous compilation cannot
+leave those checks running through the generic fallback.
+
+`nv2a_depth_reuse` counts actual GPU API submissions while replaying sixteen
+native depth-tested, read-only `LightDraw` batches against their sampled depth
+buffer. They must share one depth-view conversion, preserving all sixteen
+indexed light draws and the illuminated output pixel. Before the invalidation
+fix, this replay submitted sixteen conversions. It also requires invalidation
+after submitted depth/stencil writers and explicit clears, validates the changed
+depth pixel, and checks reuse for stencil `KEEP`, a zero stencil write mask,
+disabled depth tests, color-only clears and empty clear rectangles. Changed
+depth-view sampling metadata must still rebuild the cached view.
+
+`nv2a_world_lighting` replays the installed game's eight-stage `LightApplyTex`
+combiner. It checks that a local-light patch remains visible with zero/low base
+lighting across material alpha values, while emissive pixels, authored bright
+daylight, and output alpha remain correct. Its shader constants/register words
+were captured from the 16 October 2026 player-front night frame.
+
+`nv2a_light_volume` replays the actual one-stage `LightDraw` combiner and texture
+program `0x6C621`: scene-depth sampling, two matrix-dot padding stages, and a
+three-coordinate matrix-dot volume lookup. Its independently encoded DXT5 volume
+has a bright center, dark XY perimeter and dark Z ends. It checks the resulting
+attenuation, scene-depth occlusion and RGB-only output mask. A narrow Z interval
+also detects accidentally reconstructing local lights from fog-stretched depth.
+It alternates raw/fog views without changing depth generation, tests a changed
+fog remap, and verifies the local-light view independently: R stays one, while G
+and B hold the high and low bytes of the raw depth word. Combining those bytes
+must reproduce the raw word, including after switching between fog and light
+views of the same depth generation. The `(1, hi/255, lo/255)` view makes the
+native matrix-dot reconstruction equal `a + s * word/65536`, retaining light
+translation independently of scene depth. It samples a non-square 8x4x2 mip chain
+ending in 4x2x1. A one-deep volume must stay a 3D resource distinct from a 2D
+texture at the same address.
+An uncompressed 4x2x2 Morton volume additionally exercises projective 3D sampling
+and distinct RGB channels in each Z slice, detecting channel/order errors hidden
+by the grayscale attenuation fields.
+
+A second DXT5 field is asymmetric in X, Y and Z to catch swapped source axes.
+Ground-plane reconstruction rows then rotate its forward footprint through eight
+cardinal/diagonal headings, with centered and translated source positions. Pixel
+readback requires illumination ahead and darkness at the same distance to either
+side and behind, checking signed reconstruction terms and source translation.
+
+The retail row-builder replay reconstructs a wall 30 m from the camera through a
+light offset 4 m right and 3 m down, at 0/30/60-degree yaw. An independent
+camera-space calculation classifies wall pixels inside and outside the authored
+volume, excluding a margin around its boundary. The two-pixel sampling grid
+checks 20/8/4 illuminated pixels respectively, with at least four illuminated and
+100 dark pixels required at each yaw.
+
+A separate forward-volume replay moves the emitter from 2 m ahead through the
+camera plane to 4 m behind it, while its 50 m volume reaches a visible wall
+25 m ahead. No model or lens geometry is drawn. Independent world-space tests
+require both illuminated and dark wall samples at every source position, plus
+unchanged scene alpha. This verifies renderer support for an offscreen source;
+vehicle traversal and source retention are tested separately by the title.
+
+A linear DXT5 attenuation field sweeps 25 overlapping source positions through
+the native additive blend. Pixel readback checks independent RGB sums, both draw
+orders, continuous intensity changes and preserved scene alpha. It repeats with
+the title's optional eased attenuation enabled. That renderer policy applies
+`smoothstep(0, 1, attenuation)` only to native `LightDraw` volume alpha, retaining
+the source transforms, RGB and zero/full endpoints. It is off by default for
+toolkit callers and native replay; MM3 opts in during world-lighting setup.
+Independent profile checks require quarter/half/three-quarter strengths of
+40/128/215 out of 255 and unchanged zero/full endpoints.
+
+The title's separate overlap opt-in changes only native `LightDraw` additive RGB
+to screen accumulation: `source + destination * (1 - source)`. Equivalently, the
+result is `1 - product(1 - source)` per channel. A light over black retains its
+original brightness, while crowded intersections approach their maximum smoothly
+instead of clipping after a few overlapping beams. The hardware blend unit does
+this in the existing draw, with no extra texture, pass or source-count exposure.
+Output alpha, masks, unrelated shaders and default native replay retain guest
+state. GPU readback checks 1/2/4/8/16/32 differently colored overlapping sources
+against an independent product reference, reversed draw order, progressive
+brightening, unchanged isolated lighting, both attenuation modes, additive opt-out,
+an unrelated combiner, and alpha-writing native draws. The tolerance allows the
+existing UNORM8 buffer's rounding after each draw.
+
+Neighboring scene depths also straddle a high/low-byte carry, from `0x3ff8` to
+`0x4008`. Nine bilinear taps reconstruct that depth through the native matrix-dot
+stages and a magnified linear attenuation ramp. They must remain monotonic and
+close to their independently calculated values, detecting a point-filtered or
+independently rounded packed-depth discontinuity.
+
+Disabling the local-light byte encoding in a temporary renderer copy makes this
+row replay fail an illuminated-pixel assertion at all four MSAA/scale settings,
+confirming that coverage changes preserve detection of the depth reconstruction
+regression.
+
+Optional local validation against extracted retail attenuation volumes:
+
+```text
+nv2a_light_volume 1 1 LightVolume_Point.dds LightVolume_Spot.dds
+nv2a_light_volume 1 1 LightVolume_Point.dds LightVolume_Spot.dds 1
+```
+
+The final `1` enables pixel shader specialization. The DDS files must be the
+installed game's 32x32x32 DXT5 volumes with four mips, retaining native compressed
+block ordering. These copyrighted assets are not included in this fixture.
+The retail Point center alpha is 255 and its Z-edge axis alpha is 13; Spot center
+alpha is 173, first-slice axis alpha is 254, and last-slice alpha is zero. RGB is
+black in these attenuation assets. Correct native ordering groups up to four Z
+slices inside each XY DXT block; ordinary slice-major and 3D Morton decoding do
+not reproduce those samples or the assets' symmetry.
+
+Retail validation additionally samples 25 radial positions of each volume with
+linear filtering, requiring a gradual decrease from center to edge in both native
+and eased modes. Each eased sample must match its independently calculated
+profile. The point's sampled edge falls from 16/255 to 3/255; its full center
+stays 255/255. The spot's sampled center changes from 173/255 to 193/255 and its
+edge remains zero. Source color gains are controlled separately by the title.
+
+On 16 October 2026 the original renderer failed the native LightDraw center
+assertion with black output, because it discarded the third coordinate and
+uploaded a 2D slice. A second control retaining 3D upload but disabling raw local
+depth selection also failed that assertion. The corrected renderer passed all
+four MSAA/scale configurations, the optional retail samples, and specialization.
diff --git a/tests/nv2a_world_lighting/test_depth_reuse.c b/tests/nv2a_world_lighting/test_depth_reuse.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3a29ef2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/nv2a_world_lighting/test_depth_reuse.c
@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@
+/* Count real production submissions without adding counters to the renderer. */
+#define COBJMACROS
+#define WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
+#include <windows.h>
+#include <d3d11_1.h>
+static void counted_draw(ID3D11DeviceContext *, UINT, UINT);
+static void counted_draw_indexed(ID3D11DeviceContext *, UINT, UINT, INT);
+#undef ID3D11DeviceContext_Draw
+#undef ID3D11DeviceContext_DrawIndexed
+#define ID3D11DeviceContext_Draw counted_draw
+#define ID3D11DeviceContext_DrawIndexed counted_draw_indexed
+#define LIGHT_VOLUME_MAIN light_volume_fixture_main
+#include "test_light_volume.c"
+
+static unsigned depth_conversions, indexed_draws;
+
+static void counted_draw(ID3D11DeviceContext *context, UINT vertices, UINT first)
+{
+    if (s_bound_ps == s_y16d_ps[0] || s_bound_ps == s_y16d_ps[1])
+        ++depth_conversions;
+    context->lpVtbl->Draw(context, vertices, first);
+}
+
+static void counted_draw_indexed(ID3D11DeviceContext *context, UINT indices,
+                                  UINT first, INT base)
+{
+    ++indexed_draws;
+    context->lpVtbl->DrawIndexed(context, indices, first, base);
+}
+
+int main(int argc, char **argv)
+{
+    NvD3DState st = {0};
+    Surface *target;
+    Depth *depth;
+    uint32_t gw, gh, zmax, generation;
+    unsigned i, conversions;
+    ram = calloc(1, 0x400000); CHECK(ram);
+    _putenv_s("RECOMP_MSAA", argc > 1 ? argv[1] : "1");
+    _putenv_s("RECOMP_RENDER_SCALE", argc > 2 ? argv[2] : "1");
+    _putenv_s("RECOMP_PS_SPEC", argc > 3 ? argv[3] : "0");
+    _putenv_s("RECOMP_PS_PREWARM", "0");
+    _putenv_s("RECOMP_FPS_LIMIT", "0");
+    CHECK(nv2a_d3d_init());
+    st.color_addr = 0x10000; st.zeta_addr = 0x80000;
+    st.color_pitch = st.zeta_pitch = 256; st.surface_format = 0x28;
+    st.clip_w = st.clip_h = 64; st.color_mask = 0x10101;
+    st.depth_test = 1; st.depth_func = 0x203;
+    st.blend_enable = 1; st.blend_sfactor = st.blend_dfactor = 1;
+    st.blend_equation = 0x8006;
+    native_light_state(&st);
+    st.tex[0].addr = st.zeta_addr; st.tex[0].color = 0x35;
+    st.tex[0].width = 128; st.tex[0].height = 64; st.tex[0].pitch = 256;
+    st.tex[0].levels = 1; st.tex[0].filter = 0x02062000;
+    st.tex[3].addr = 0x100000; st.tex[3].color = 0x0F;
+    st.tex[3].width = st.tex[3].height = st.tex[3].depth = 32;
+    st.tex[3].format = (5u<<28) | (5u<<24) | (5u<<20) | (0xFu<<8) | (3u<<4);
+    st.tex[3].levels = 1; st.tex[3].filter = 0x01010000;
+    st.tex[3].address = 0x30303;
+    CHECK(make_field(ram + 0x100000, 32, 32, 32, 1) == 32768);
+    nv2a_d3d_clear(&st, 0xF1, 0xA5000000, 0x40000000, 0, 0, 63, 63);
+    fixture_prepare_shader(&st);
+    nv2a_d3d_clear(&st, 1, 0, 0x40000000, 0, 0, 63, 63);
+    depth = depth_find(st.zeta_addr); CHECK(depth);
+    generation = depth->gen;
+    depth_conversions = indexed_draws = 0;
+    /* Actual captured LightDraw state: depth test LEQUAL, depth writes off.
+     * Count each conversion and indexed submission through the GPU API. */
+    for (i = 0; i < 16; ++i) light_draw(&st, .5f, .5f, .5f, .25f, .125f);
+    printf("read-only LightDraw: %u indexed draws, %u depth conversions\n",
+           indexed_draws, depth_conversions);
+    CHECK(indexed_draws == 16 && depth_conversions == 1);
+    CHECK(depth->gen == generation && depth->y16_gen == generation);
+    target = surface_find(st.color_addr); CHECK(target);
+    CHECK((pixel(target, (unsigned)(32 * target->sx), (unsigned)(32 * target->sy)) & 0xFFFFFFu) == 0xFFFFFFu);
+    CHECK(setup_pipeline(&st, NV_D3D_TRIANGLES, &target, &gw, &gh, &zmax));
+    CHECK(setup_pipeline(&st, NV_D3D_TRIANGLES, &target, &gw, &gh, &zmax));
+    CHECK(depth->gen == generation && depth_conversions == 1);
+    /* View metadata can change without a write. A changed guest-width
+     * half-texel correction must still rebuild, then become reusable. */
+    depth->w /= 2;
+    CHECK(depth_y16_view(depth, 2)); CHECK(depth_conversions == 2);
+    CHECK(depth_y16_view(depth, 2)); CHECK(depth_conversions == 2);
+    depth->w *= 2;
+    CHECK(depth_y16_view(depth, 2)); CHECK(depth_conversions == 3);
+
+    /* A submitted depth writer must invalidate immediately, including the
+     * case where the draw read the same depth view before writing. */
+    st.depth_mask = 1;
+    light_draw(&st, .5f, .5f, .5f, .25f, .125f);
+    CHECK(depth->gen == generation + 1);
+    conversions = depth_conversions;
+    CHECK(depth_y16_view(depth, 1));
+    CHECK(depth_conversions == conversions + 1);
+    CHECK(depth_word(depth) >= 8190 && depth_word(depth) <= 8193);
+    st.depth_mask = 0;
+
+    /* Masked-out stencil writes and KEEP operations are read-only too. */
+    st.stencil_test = 1; st.stencil_func = 0x207;
+    st.stencil_func_mask = 0xFF; st.stencil_ref = 7;
+    st.stencil_fail = st.stencil_zfail = st.stencil_zpass = 0x1E00;
+    st.stencil_write_mask = 0xFF;
+    generation = depth->gen;
+    light_draw(&st, .5f, .5f, .5f, .125f, .0625f);
+    CHECK(depth->gen == generation);
+    st.stencil_zpass = 0x1E01; st.stencil_write_mask = 0;
+    light_draw(&st, .5f, .5f, .5f, .125f, .0625f);
+    CHECK(depth->gen == generation);
+    st.stencil_write_mask = 0xFF;
+    light_draw(&st, .5f, .5f, .5f, .125f, .0625f);
+    CHECK(depth->gen == generation + 1);
+    conversions = depth_conversions;
+    CHECK(depth_y16_view(depth, 2));
+    CHECK(depth_conversions == conversions + 1);
+    st.stencil_test = 0;
+    st.depth_test = 0; st.depth_mask = 1;
+    generation = depth->gen;
+    light_draw(&st, .5f, .5f, .5f, .125f, .0625f);
+    CHECK(depth->gen == generation); /* disabled tests cannot write depth */
+    st.depth_test = 1; st.depth_mask = 0;
+
+    /* Explicit clears write regardless of the guest draw's write masks.
+     * Color-only clears and empty rectangles must preserve the depth view. */
+    generation = depth->gen;
+    nv2a_d3d_clear(&st, 0xF0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 63, 63);
+    CHECK(depth->gen == generation);
+    nv2a_d3d_clear(&st, 1, 0, 0, 64, 64, 63, 63);
+    CHECK(depth->gen == generation);
+    nv2a_d3d_clear(&st, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 63, 63);
+    CHECK(depth->gen == generation + 1);
+    generation = depth->gen;
+    nv2a_d3d_clear(&st, 1, 0, 0x60000000, 0, 0, 63, 63);
+    CHECK(depth->gen == generation + 1);
+    CHECK(depth_y16_view(depth, 1));
+    CHECK(depth_word(depth) >= 24574 && depth_word(depth) <= 24577);
+    puts("PASS: read-only depth reuse and submitted depth/stencil draw/clear invalidation");
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/nv2a_world_lighting/test_light_volume.c b/tests/nv2a_world_lighting/test_light_volume.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..21ac01a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/nv2a_world_lighting/test_light_volume.c
@@ -0,0 +1,824 @@
+/* GPU replay of MM3's native Light/LightDraw.psh texture program. */
+#define main composite_fixture_main
+#include "test_world_lighting.c"
+#undef main
+
+/* Captured night player/street LightDraw: tex t0; texm3x3pad t1,t0;
+ * texm3x3pad t2,t0; texm3x3tex t3,t0; mul r0,v0,t3.a.
+ * Actual FTRACE: out/night-lighting-qa/night-stderr.log, 16 October 2026.
+ * Only reconstruction rows, depth and attenuation texels are controlled. */
+static void native_light_state(NvD3DState *st)
+{
+    st->rc_seen = 1; st->rc.control = 0x11101;
+    st->rc.stage_program = 0x6C621;
+    st->rc.final0 = 0x0000000C; st->rc.final1 = 0x00001B80;
+    st->rc.color_icw[0] = 0xC4DB0000;
+    st->rc.alpha_icw[0] = 0xD4DB1010;
+    st->rc.color_ocw[0] = st->rc.alpha_ocw[0] = 0xC0;
+}
+
+/* LightDraw reads the scene depth as (1, high byte, low byte) of the 16-bit
+ * word z[23:8], each as byte/255, and its texcoord rows are
+ * (a, 255/256 * s, 255/65536 * s): a + s * word/65536 -- see y16d_ps. */
+#define ROW_HI 0.99609381f
+#define ROW_LO 0.0038909914f
+
+/* The 16-bit word the renderer stores for a cleared depth fraction, as a
+ * fraction of 65536: what the dot product multiplies s by. */
+static float depth_fraction(float scene_depth)
+{
+    uint32_t z24 = (uint32_t)(scene_depth * 16777215.0f);
+    return (float)(z24 >> 8) / 65536.0f;
+}
+
+/* A row whose dot product with the depth view is `target` when the scene is
+ * at `scene_depth`: half from the constant, half from the depth term. */
+static void depth_row(float row[4], float target, float scene_depth)
+{
+    float a = target * 0.5f, s = target * 0.5f / depth_fraction(scene_depth);
+    row[0] = a; row[1] = s * ROW_HI; row[2] = s * ROW_LO; row[3] = 1;
+}
+
+static void light_draw_sample(const NvD3DState *st, float x, float y, float z,
+                              float scene_depth, float draw_depth, float depth_x,
+                              uint32_t color, const float z_row[4])
+{
+    const uint32_t indices[] = {0,1,2,2,1,3};
+    float position[4][4] = {{0,0,0,1},{64,0,0,1},{0,64,0,1},{64,64,0,1}};
+    float defaults[16][4] = {{0}};
+    NvD3DAttrib attr[16] = {{0}};
+    unsigned n;
+    for (n = 0; n < 4; ++n) position[n][2] = draw_depth * 16777215.0f;
+    attr[0].enabled = 1; attr[0].type = 2; attr[0].size = 4;
+    attr[0].stride = sizeof position[0]; attr[0].data = (const uint8_t *)position;
+    unpack4(color, defaults[3]);
+    defaults[9][0] = depth_x; defaults[9][1] = 32; defaults[9][3] = 1;
+    /* These rows reconstruct a chosen 3D voxel through the actual native dot
+     * pipeline, with the constant and the depth term both contributing. */
+    depth_row(defaults[10], x, scene_depth);
+    depth_row(defaults[11], y, scene_depth);
+    depth_row(defaults[12], z, scene_depth);
+    if (z_row) memcpy(defaults[12], z_row, sizeof defaults[12]);
+    fixture_prepare_shader(st);
+    nv2a_d3d_draw_ub(st, NV_D3D_TRIANGLES, attr, defaults, 0, indices, 6, 0, 3, NULL);
+}
+
+static void light_draw(const NvD3DState *st, float x, float y, float z,
+                       float scene_depth, float draw_depth)
+{
+    light_draw_sample(st,x,y,z,scene_depth,draw_depth,65,0xFFFFFFFFu,NULL);
+}
+
+static int sample_light(NvD3DState *st, Surface *target, const char *name,
+                        float x, float y, float z, unsigned expected,
+                        float depth)
+{
+    uint32_t value;
+    unsigned c;
+    nv2a_d3d_clear(st, 0xF1, 0xA5000000, (uint32_t)(.25f * 16777215.0f) << 8, 0,0,63,63);
+    light_draw(st, x,y,z,.25f,depth);
+    value = pixel(target, (unsigned)(32 * target->sx), (unsigned)(32 * target->sy));
+    c = value & 255;
+    printf("%s xyz=%.5f,%.5f,%.5f pixel=%08X expected=%u\n", name,x,y,z,value,expected);
+    CHECK((value >> 24) == 0xA5);
+    CHECK(((value >> 16) & 255) == c && ((value >> 8) & 255) == c);
+    CHECK(c + 2 >= expected && c <= expected + 2);
+    return 0;
+}
+
+/* Independent authored fixture: a central illuminated cuboid, with dark XY
+ * perimeter and three eighths of Z at either end. Encoding follows the retail block
+ * grouping, not the renderer's decoder. Every DXT5 block has constant alpha. */
+static size_t make_field(uint8_t *dst, unsigned w, unsigned h, unsigned d, unsigned levels)
+{
+    size_t offset = 0;
+    unsigned lv;
+    for (lv = 0; lv < levels; ++lv) {
+        unsigned bw = (w + 3) / 4, bh = (h + 3) / 4, group;
+        for (group = 0; group < d; group += 4) {
+            unsigned by,bx,dz,count = d-group < 4 ? d-group : 4;
+            for (by = 0; by < bh; ++by) for (bx = 0; bx < bw; ++bx)
+                for (dz = 0; dz < count; ++dz) {
+                    unsigned alpha = lv ? 91 : (bx && bx+1 < bw && by && by+1 < bh &&
+                        group+dz >= 3*d/8 && group+dz < 5*d/8 ? 255 : 0);
+                    memset(dst+offset, 0, 16);
+                    dst[offset] = dst[offset+1] = (uint8_t)alpha;
+                    offset += 16;
+                }
+        }
+        w = w > 1 ? w/2 : 1; h = h > 1 ? h/2 : 1; d = d > 1 ? d/2 : 1;
+    }
+    return offset;
+}
+
+/* Independent linear alpha ramp through Z, encoded in the native four-slice
+ * DXT5 grouping. Trilinear sampling inside the volume should reconstruct
+ * alpha = Z, including between authored slices. */
+static void make_gradient_field(uint8_t *dst)
+{
+    unsigned group, by, bx, dz;
+    size_t offset = 0;
+    for (group = 0; group < 32; group += 4)
+        for (by = 0; by < 8; ++by) for (bx = 0; bx < 8; ++bx)
+            for (dz = 0; dz < 4; ++dz) {
+                unsigned alpha = (unsigned)((group + dz + .5f) * (255.0f / 32) + .5f);
+                memset(dst + offset,0,16);
+                dst[offset] = dst[offset + 1] = (uint8_t)alpha;
+                offset += 16;
+            }
+}
+
+static int check_light_overlap(NvD3DState st, Surface *target)
+{
+    unsigned step, order, shift, soft;
+#ifndef VOLUME_OLD_RENDERER
+    const unsigned modes = 2;
+#else
+    const unsigned modes = 1;
+#endif
+    make_gradient_field(ram + 0x100000);
+    nv2a_d3d_kick();
+    st.tex[3].filter = 0x02020000; /* linear min/mag; authored mip 0 */
+    st.blend_enable = 1; st.blend_sfactor = st.blend_dfactor = 1;
+    st.blend_equation = 0x8006;
+    /* Two differently colored lights overlap at every step. Their strengths
+     * vary smoothly in opposite directions. Additive RGB must be independent
+     * of draw order and alpha must retain its scene sentinel. */
+    for (soft = 0; soft < modes; ++soft) {
+      unsigned previous = 0;
+#ifndef VOLUME_OLD_RENDERER
+      nv2a_d3d_set_local_light_softness(soft);
+#endif
+      for (step = 0; step <= 24; ++step) {
+        float z[2] = {.125f + step / 32.0f, .875f - step / 32.0f};
+        static const uint32_t colors[2] = {0xFF804020u,0xFF203040u};
+        uint32_t result[2];
+        for (order = 0; order < 2; ++order) {
+            unsigned n;
+            nv2a_d3d_clear(&st,0xF1,0xA5000000,
+                (uint32_t)(.25f * 16777215.0f) << 8,0,0,63,63);
+            for (n = 0; n < 2; ++n) {
+                unsigned source = n ^ order;
+                light_draw_sample(&st,.5f,.5f,z[source],.25f,.125f,65,colors[source],NULL);
+            }
+            result[order] = pixel(target,(unsigned)(32 * target->sx),(unsigned)(32 * target->sy));
+            CHECK((result[order] >> 24) == 0xA5);
+        }
+        CHECK(result[0] == result[1]);
+        for (shift = 0; shift < 24; shift += 8) {
+            unsigned c = (result[0] >> shift) & 255;
+            float strength[2] = {z[0],z[1]}, expected;
+            if (soft) {
+                unsigned n;
+                for (n = 0; n < 2; ++n)
+                    strength[n] = strength[n] * strength[n] * (3 - 2 * strength[n]);
+            }
+            expected = ((colors[0] >> shift) & 255) * strength[0] +
+                       ((colors[1] >> shift) & 255) * strength[1];
+            CHECK(fabsf((float)c - expected) <= 2.0f);
+        }
+        /* Red increases about three byte values per step: no disappearing
+         * contribution, large jump, or quantized 3D attenuation staircase. */
+        if (step) {
+            unsigned red = (result[0] >> 16) & 255;
+            CHECK(red > previous && red <= previous + 7);
+        }
+        previous = (result[0] >> 16) & 255;
+      }
+      printf("PASS: 25 overlapping gradient positions add smoothly in either draw order and preserve scene alpha (softness=%u)\n",soft);
+    }
+#ifndef VOLUME_OLD_RENDERER
+    nv2a_d3d_set_local_light_softness(0);
+#endif
+    return 0;
+}
+
+#ifndef VOLUME_OLD_RENDERER
+/* Independent overlap reference: each source adds its RGB in proportion to
+ * the headroom remaining at this pixel. Source count elsewhere is irrelevant. */
+static int check_bounded_light_overlap(NvD3DState st, Surface *target)
+{
+    static const unsigned counts[] = {1,2,4,8,16,32};
+    static const uint32_t colors[] = {0xFF806040u,0xFF204080u,0xFF603020u};
+    unsigned soft, group, order, n, shift;
+    make_gradient_field(ram + 0x100000);
+    nv2a_d3d_kick();
+    st.tex[3].filter = 0x02020000;
+    st.blend_enable = 1; st.blend_sfactor = st.blend_dfactor = 1;
+    st.blend_equation = 0x8006;
+    for (soft = 0; soft < 2; ++soft) {
+        unsigned previous[3] = {0};
+        nv2a_d3d_set_local_light_softness(soft);
+        for (group = 0; group < sizeof counts / sizeof counts[0]; ++group) {
+            unsigned count = counts[group];
+            uint32_t results[2];
+            float reference[3] = {1,1,1};
+            for (n = 0; n < count; ++n) {
+                float a = .25f + .125f * (n % 3);
+                if (soft) a = a * a * (3 - 2 * a);
+                for (shift = 0; shift < 24; shift += 8)
+                    reference[shift / 8] *= 1 - a * ((colors[n % 3] >> shift) & 255) / 255.0f;
+            }
+            nv2a_d3d_set_local_light_overlap(1);
+            for (order = 0; order < 2; ++order) {
+                NvD3DState right = st;
+                nv2a_d3d_clear(&st,0xF1,0xA5000000,
+                    (uint32_t)(.25f * 16777215.0f) << 8,0,0,63,63);
+                /* This isolated light is present once, no matter how many
+                 * sources overlap in the right-hand intersection. */
+                light_draw_sample(&st,.5f,.5f,.375f,.25f,.125f,65,0xFF406080u,NULL);
+                right.clip_x = 32; right.clip_w = 32;
+                /* Clear only the crowded half, retaining the isolated lamp. */
+                nv2a_d3d_clear(&right,0xF0,0xA5000000,0,32,0,63,63);
+                for (n = 0; n < count; ++n) {
+                    unsigned source = order ? count - n - 1 : n;
+                    light_draw_sample(&right,.5f,.5f,.25f + .125f * (source % 3),
+                        .25f,.125f,65,colors[source % 3],NULL);
+                }
+                results[order] = pixel(target,(unsigned)(48 * target->sx),(unsigned)(32 * target->sy));
+                CHECK((results[order] >> 24) == 0xA5);
+                {
+                    uint32_t isolated = pixel(target,(unsigned)(16 * target->sx),(unsigned)(32 * target->sy));
+                    float a = soft ? .31640625f : .375f;
+                    CHECK((isolated >> 24) == 0xA5);
+                    for (shift = 0; shift < 24; shift += 8)
+                        CHECK(fabsf((float)((isolated >> shift) & 255) -
+                            a * ((0xFF406080u >> shift) & 255)) <= 2);
+                }
+            }
+            for (shift = 0; shift < 24; shift += 8) {
+                unsigned c = (results[0] >> shift) & 255;
+                unsigned reverse = (results[1] >> shift) & 255;
+                float expected = 255 * (1 - reference[shift / 8]);
+                /* UNORM8 rounds after each draw. Reversing a long chain may
+                 * differ slightly, but cannot change its perceived energy. */
+                CHECK(fabsf((float)c - expected) <= 4);
+                CHECK(abs((int)c - (int)reverse) <= 3);
+                CHECK(c > previous[shift / 8]);
+                CHECK(c < 254); /* no premature white clipping */
+                previous[shift / 8] = c;
+            }
+            printf("bounded-overlap soft=%u sources=%u rgb=%06X reverse=%06X\n",
+                soft,count,results[0] & 0xFFFFFF,results[1] & 0xFFFFFF);
+        }
+    }
+    nv2a_d3d_set_local_light_softness(0);
+    /* Opting out retains native additive accumulation. Opting in must also
+     * leave a different register-combiner draw and native alpha unaffected. */
+    for (group = 0; group < 3; ++group) {
+        NvD3DState control = st;
+        uint32_t result;
+        nv2a_d3d_set_local_light_overlap(group != 0);
+        if (group == 1) control.rc.control ^= 0x10u;
+        if (group == 2) control.color_mask = 0x1010101u;
+        nv2a_d3d_clear(&control,0xF1,0x11000000,
+            (uint32_t)(.25f * 16777215.0f) << 8,0,0,63,63);
+        for (n = 0; n < 2; ++n)
+            light_draw_sample(&control,.5f,.5f,.5f,.25f,.125f,65,0xFF808080u,NULL);
+        result = pixel(target,(unsigned)(32 * target->sx),(unsigned)(32 * target->sy));
+        printf("overlap-control mode=%u pixel=%08X\n",group,result);
+        if (group == 2) {
+            CHECK((result >> 24) == 255); /* guest ONE/ONE alpha, not screen */
+            CHECK((result & 255) >= 110 && (result & 255) <= 114);
+        } else {
+            CHECK((result >> 24) == 0x11);
+            CHECK((result & 255) >= 126 && (result & 255) <= 130);
+        }
+    }
+    nv2a_d3d_set_local_light_overlap(0);
+    puts("PASS: bounded RGB overlap preserves isolated sources, draw-order stability, native alpha and unrelated draws");
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static int check_soft_profile(NvD3DState st, Surface *target)
+{
+    static const float positions[5] = {0,.25f,.5f,.75f,1};
+    /* Independent expected eased values: 0, 5/32, 1/2, 27/32, 1. */
+    static const unsigned expected[5] = {0,40,128,215,255};
+    unsigned n;
+    nv2a_d3d_set_local_light_softness(1);
+    CHECK(make_field(ram + 0x100000,32,32,32,1) == 32768);
+    nv2a_d3d_kick();
+    CHECK(!sample_light(&st,target,"soft-full-endpoint",.5f,.5f,.5f,255,.125f));
+    CHECK(!sample_light(&st,target,"soft-zero-endpoint",0,.5f,.5f,0,.125f));
+    make_gradient_field(ram + 0x100000);
+    nv2a_d3d_kick();
+    st.tex[3].filter = 0x02020000;
+    for (n = 0; n < 5; ++n)
+        CHECK(!sample_light(&st,target,"soft-gradient",.5f,.5f,positions[n],expected[n],.125f));
+    nv2a_d3d_set_local_light_softness(0);
+    puts("PASS: opt-in eased attenuation retains zero/full endpoints and expected quarter/half/three-quarter strengths");
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static int check_depth_byte_interpolation(NvD3DState st, Surface *target)
+{
+    Depth *depth;
+    unsigned step, previous = 0;
+    /* Adjacent scene depths straddle a high-byte carry: (63,248) and
+     * (64,8). Their reconstructed depths differ by just 16/65536. The large
+     * Z scale exposes either independently rounded or point-filtered bytes. */
+    static const float z_row[4] = {-255.5f,1024 * ROW_HI,1024 * ROW_LO,1};
+    make_gradient_field(ram + 0x100000);
+    nv2a_d3d_kick();
+    st.tex[0].filter = st.tex[3].filter = 0x02020000;
+    nv2a_d3d_clear(&st,0xF1,0xA5000000,0x3FF80000u,0,0,63,63);
+    nv2a_d3d_clear(&st,0x01,0,0x40080000u,32,0,63,63);
+    depth = depth_find(st.zeta_addr); CHECK(depth);
+    for (step = 0; step <= 8; ++step) {
+        float weight = step / 8.0f;
+        float scale = (float)depth->iw / depth->w;
+        /* Independent y16d_ps addressing: first right-hand texel after the
+         * quarter-guest-pixel depth-view shift. Sample across that boundary. */
+        float boundary = ceilf(depth->iw + .5f * scale - .5f);
+        float depth_x = (boundary - .5f + weight) / scale;
+        uint32_t value;
+        unsigned c;
+        nv2a_d3d_clear(&st,0xF0,0xA5000000,0,0,0,63,63);
+        light_draw_sample(&st,.5f,.5f,.5f,.25f,.125f,depth_x,0xFFFFFFFFu,z_row);
+        value = pixel(target,(unsigned)(32 * target->sx),(unsigned)(32 * target->sy));
+        c = value & 255;
+        printf("depth-byte carry weight=%.3f rgb=%u expected=%.2f\n",weight,c,255 * (.375f + .25f * weight));
+        CHECK((value >> 24) == 0xA5);
+        CHECK(fabsf((float)c - 255 * (.375f + .25f * weight)) <= 2.0f);
+        if (step) CHECK(c > previous && c <= previous + 13);
+        previous = c;
+    }
+    puts("PASS: bilinear high/low depth bytes reconstruct smoothly across a byte carry");
+    return 0;
